<%#
  The drawing and the words that go with it (WP9). One partial rather than two so
  that a caller can put both behind the same disclosure: on a workflow so
  permissive that the picture has no shape to show (finding F03), the drawing is
  collapsed and a legend left behind above it would explain arrows nobody can
  see.

  Locals: layout.
%>
<%= render partial: 'project_workflows/graph_svg', locals: { layout: layout } %>

<%# Only the sentences that are about something on the page. The helper says
    why. %>
<% legend = project_workflow_graph_legend(layout) %>
<% if legend.any? %>
  <p class="project-workflow-graph-legend">
    <em><%= legend.join(' ') %></em>
  </p>
<% end %>
